strata$ forth < nettest.fs
Strata Forth 0.1 (native code, 1 thread, StrataOS 0.1) N code bytes free, N data bytes free
\ Strata Forth under StrataOS: the network words, over loopback (no link needed).  ok
\ Fed to `forth < nettest.fs` by tests/run-os.sh; expected output: tests/net.out.  ok
\ ---- at the prompt each word loads net.fs (or udp.fs) for one command  ok
s" 10.0.0.1" str>ip h.  s" 1.2.3" str>ip .  s" 1.2.3.256" str>ip .  s" 1.2.3.4.5" str>ip . $a000001 -1 -1 -1  ok
$7f000001 .ip  $0a000102 ip>str type 127.0.0.1 10.0.1.2 ok
$7f000001 ping 0> . net: 10.0.0.1, no link
-1  ok
[defined] tcp-listen .  [defined] net.fs . 0 0  ok
\ ---- for good: TCP within one process (a connection is established before it is accepted)  ok
require udp  [defined] tcp-listen .  [defined] udp-open .  [defined] net.fs . -1 -1 -1  ok
variable lsn  variable cli  variable srv  create buf 64 allot  ok
7000 tcp-listen dup lsn ! 0> .  7000 tcp-listen . -1 -7  ok
$7f000001 7000 tcp-connect dup cli ! 0> . -1  ok
lsn @ tcp-accept dup srv ! 0> . -1  ok
s" hello, strata" cli @ sock-write . 13  ok
buf 64 srv @ sock-read buf swap type hello, strata ok
srv @ sock-peer 49151 > . .ip -1 127.0.0.1  ok
s" and back" srv @ sock-write .  srv @ sock-close 8  ok
buf 64 cli @ sock-read buf swap type  buf 64 cli @ sock-read . and back0  ok
cli @ sock-close  lsn @ sock-close  ok
$7f000001 7001 tcp-connect . -1  ok
\ ---- UDP  ok
0 udp-open dup cli ! 0> .  7001 udp-open dup srv ! 0> . -1 -1  ok
s" a datagram" $7f000001 7001 cli @ udp-send . 10  ok
buf 64 srv @ udp-recv 49151 > . .ip buf swap type -1 127.0.0.1 a datagram ok
cli @ sock-close  srv @ sock-close  ok
bye strata$ -n 2 forth -e 80 tcp-listen
